{"aligned_passages":[],"lenses":{},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&ref=sha256%3A264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c%2Fevidence%2Fmapping.long.thm-perturbed-family-maximality","record":{"command":[],"details":"The papers' evidence mapping names these Lean declarations for Long record Theorem 6.62 (Perturbed-family maximality and the three-branch recurrence). Long record thm:perturbed-family-maximality: lean.status exact_or_stronger. Relation note: The Lean statements have the same hypotheses and conclusions as the printed ones. Under $B<g$, `prefixChoice_maximal` bounds every admissible updated value by $t$ of the chosen element, which is admissible by `above_newSum_le_capacity_iff` when $4o+p_+\\le g$ and by `below_newSum_le_capacity` otherwise, and `prefixRemainder_eq_capacity_sub_choice` identifies the remainder before the weight $W$ with $C'$ minus that value. `nextRemainder_trichotomy` gives the three remainders, whose natural-number subtractions agree with the printed ones because $p_-\\le B<g$ and because of each case's inequality. Sources: evidence/paper_evidence.json at 3368d1e69467. Scope: copied from the papers' evidence mapping; this example did not review the correspondence.","id":"mapping.long.thm-perturbed-family-maximality","kind":"semantic_review","source_ids":["evidence_mapping"],"status":"not_run","subject_ids":["lean.Erdos249257.HalfCylinderIntegerGreedy.PerturbedFamily.AdjacentCut.above_newSum_le_capacity_iff","lean.Erdos249257.HalfCylinderIntegerGreedy.PerturbedFamily.AdjacentCut.below_newSum_le_capacity","lean.Erdos249257.HalfCylinderIntegerGreedy.PerturbedFamily.AdjacentCut.nextRemainder_trichotomy","lean.Erdos249257.HalfCylinderIntegerGreedy.PerturbedFamily.AdjacentCut.prefixChoice_maximal","lean.Erdos249257.HalfCylinderIntegerGreedy.PerturbedFamily.AdjacentCut.prefixRemainder_eq_capacity_sub_choice","long.thm-perturbed-family-maxi